`epppsynth/templates/**` and `epppsynth/schemas/**` are named in the licence
boundary EP-5 fixed: templates are CC BY 4.0 because their value is the wording
(D-50), and schemas are Apache-2.0. Neither directory exists yet, and a
`REUSE.toml` path that matches no file is a REUSE error, so their annotations
are added by the brief that first creates them (`epppsynth/registry/` schemas —
planned EP-9; `epppsynth/templates/` — planned EP-11).

`LICENSE` and `LICENSES/**` carry no annotation of their own. They are verbatim
third-party licence texts, reproduced under the terms each licence states for
its own reproduction. `epppsynth.rights.coverage` records them as a named
exemption rather than passing over them silently.


2. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
=======================

No third-party source code is vendored into this repository. There is no
bundled library, no minified asset, and no copied implementation. `htmx` is
planned for vendoring when the web UI is built (0BSD, with its path, version
and SHA-256 recorded here at that point — planned EP-40); nothing is vendored
today.

One third-party *text* is reproduced verbatim, and CC BY 4.0 requires that its
attribution travel with it:

    Contributor Covenant, version 2.1
    Copyright 2014 Coraline Ada Ehmke and the Contributor Covenant contributors
    https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/2/1/code_of_conduct.html
    Licensed under CC BY 4.0

    Reproduced at `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md` unedited apart from the contact address
    and a clearly separated project addendum marked as not part of the
    Covenant. Its integrity is checked against a recorded SHA-256 by
    `epppsynth/tests/test_public_docs.py`.

A CycloneDX software bill of materials and a generated
`epppsynth/docs/third-party-licenses.md` covering the dependency tree are
produced per release rather than per commit (planned EP-50). This section
covers material committed to the repository, not installed dependencies.


3. RIGHTS POSTURE FOR THE CONCEPTUAL SOURCES
============================================

The conceptual substrate of this project is read from works the author lawfully
holds. None of it is redistributed. In the sense that matters here — the
copyrighted works the concept model is built from —

    this repository contains no third-party copyrighted source text; the concept registry is original prose that cites its sources

(D-10(i)). "Source text" in that sentence means the text of a cited work. It
does not describe the Contributor Covenant of section 2, which is reproduced
under its own licence and attributed above.

The corpus lives in a gitignored directory; the derived index and any model
weights live outside the working tree entirely. None of it is tracked, enters
CI, or appears in a published artifact.

What each cited source permits — its licence, its reuse class, whether anyone
has verified its terms, and on what date — is recorded per source in

    epppsynth/docs/rights.md

which is generated from `epppsynth/registry/sources.yaml`. That table is the
authority on the sources; this file is the authority on the repository's own
licensing. Sources whose reuse terms nobody has checked appear there under a
separate heading that says so.

Public citations are chapter-level locators only, and quotation is capped at
25 words per quote and 150 words per source (D-74).


4. WHAT THIS SOFTWARE IS NOT
============================

epppsynth is not therapy, not clinical decision support, not a risk detector,
and not a source of clinical recommendations. It is not validated and is not
for clinical use. `SAFETY.md` and `epppsynth/GOVERNANCE.md` state the intended
and excluded uses; the latter binds where the two differ.
